WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.370
I'm standing on the
southern tip of Africa

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.740
and imagining what it was like
sometime in the last hundreds

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.341
of thousands of years.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:13.780
Back then, Africa was home to
all the world's Homo sapiens,

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.549
all 10,000 of them.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.719
If you were an extraterrestrial
on a survey mission,

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:23.390
you might have thought we
were an endangered species.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:27.627
Someday soon, there will
be 10 billion of us.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.862
What happened?

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.098
How did we become the globe
girdling space traveling

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.900
species that we are today?

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:46.780
Welcome to the first
laboratory on Earth.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:50.016
We're in Blombos Cave, where
the evolution of the mind

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.785
made a great leap.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:55.422
Our ancestors were conducting
chemistry experiments here with

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:59.692
a mineral rich in iron, ocher.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:03.096
They used it to decorate
objects with bits of red color,

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.365
but it may have
also had other uses.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:08.201
To preserve animal
hides or as a medicine,

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:11.905
or as a way to
sharpen their tools.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.942
Or maybe as an insect repellent.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:19.746
And they engraved the ocher with
symbols, something completely

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.415
new on the planet Earth.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.050
Art.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.787
Not to be eaten, not
to provide shelter,

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:31.591
but to symbolize something.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.626
Or just to be.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.796
Looks a little bit like
a ladder or double helix.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:40.066
Whatever it was supposed to
be, it's the earliest remnant

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.302
we have of human culture.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.071
We had found a way to
leave behind something

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.873
distinctly human.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:51.110
A means to communicate
however enigmatically to you

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:55.615
and me 100,000 years away.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:59.786
A great power was discovered
here in Blombos Cave.

